      content:
          '**Sport-Specific Conditioning Program:**\n- **Cardiovascular:** Handcycling or arm ergometry 3x/week for 30-45 minutes at 70-85% max HR. Swimming 2x/week for shoulder-friendly cross-training.\n- **Strength:** Upper body periodized program — push/pull balance. Emphasize pulling exercises (rows, reverse flys) at 2:1 ratio to pushing to counteract wheelchair propulsion imbalance. Rotator cuff pre-habilitation daily.\n- **Sport-specific:** Wheelchair sprints, starts/stops, pivoting, chair skills (wheelies, tipping recovery). Shooting drills from wheelchair.\n- **Core/trunk:** Seated balance training with perturbation, medicine ball catches and throws, trunk rotation resistance.\n\n**Shoulder Preservation Protocol:**\n- Limit total daily shoulder load: track practice hours + daily propulsion\n- Mandatory rest days: at minimum 1 full rest day per week, 2 preferred\n- Ice after every practice (15 minutes, shoulder)\n- Anti-inflammatory use: PRN ibuprofen after intense sessions (not daily to avoid GI/renal effects)\n- Stretch routine: pectoralis, anterior deltoid, posterior capsule — before and after every session\n- Annual shoulder MRI surveillance while competing\n\n**Sports Wheelchair Prescription:**\n- **Frame:** Rigid titanium or aluminum, maximum lightweight construction (typically 10-12 lbs for frame)\n- **Seat:** Lower seat height than daily chair for court access and stability. Bucket seat with 10-15 degree dump for stability during contact.\n- **Wheels:** 25-inch or 26-inch cambered wheels (12-15 degree camber for wheelchair basketball — provides lateral stability and quicker turns). High-pressure tires for speed.\n- **Anti-tip:** Rear anti-tip casters mandatory per IWBF rules. Fifth wheel (front caster) optional.\n- **Strapping:** Abdominal and thigh straps to compensate for absent trunk control. Must meet IWBF equipment rules.\n- **Customization:** Seat width, depth, and backrest height customized by certified ATP with wheelchair sports experience.\n- **Cost:** \$3,000-\$6,000 for a competitive sports wheelchair.\n\n**Medical Clearance for Competition:**\n- Pre-participation physical examination including cardiovascular screening, shoulder assessment, skin check\n- Written clearance letter for IWBF registration\n- Establish UTI prevention protocol for tournament travel (hydration plan, catheterization schedule)\n- Thermal regulation plan for summer competitions\n- Emergency action plan: autonomic dysreflexia protocol (even though L1 is below typical threshold, awareness for team medical staff)',
